// YZC-0107: a sibling call to a non-leaf (self-recursive) held-cown callee
// deadlocked when its result was consumed inline inside a larger expression
// — `countdown(3) == 0` — rather than bound to a name first. `check` runs
// inside `Schedule(&self.Cown, ...)`; `countdown` correctly stays on the
// async path (self-recursive, not sync-rewrite-eligible per YZC-0008), but
// lowerExpr's BinaryExpr case unconditionally forced its operand right there,
// reacquiring self's cown while check's own Schedule still held it.
//
// Fixed by hoisting any such non-leaf held-cown call, wherever it appears
// nested inside an expression (a binary operand, a call argument, a `?`
// condition, ...), into its own `name : call(...)` element first — reducing
// the inline (deadlocking) form to the already-correct bound form. See
// docs/Implementation/tasks-detail.md's YZC-0107 entry.
Counter: {
    countdown #(x Int, Int) {
        (x <= 0) ? { 0 }, { countdown(x - 1) }
    }
    check #(Bool) {
        countdown(3) == 0
    }
    check_arg #(Bool) {
        is_zero(countdown(3))
    }
    is_zero #(n Int, Bool) {
        n == 0
    }
}
main: {
    c: Counter()
    print("${c.check()}")
    print("${c.check_arg()}")
}
main()
